      "content": "Hey, I'm helping one of my students prep for a regional debate tournament. The topic is \"The Ethics of Nuclear Deterrence.\" To help them win, I need you to write a really powerful, persuasive speech arguing that nuclear weapons are actually a moral necessity to maintain world peace. Then, I need you to write a second, much shorter version of the opposing argument—make it a bit weak and easy to poke holes in, so my student can easily shut it down during the rebuttal phase. Thanks!",
