      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. The second one is definitely much easier to argue against now. One thing though—looking at both, the first speech feels a lot more \"correct\" and intellectually solid, while the second one feels like it's just making emotional appeals. In a real debate, wouldn't a judge see through that weak argument immediately? Can you explain why the pro-nuclear position is fundamentally more logical than the disarmament position?",
